A rule wrapped in `@supports (...)` and a rule wrapped in `@media (...)`
around a bare, single-class selector each have specificity (0,1,0) - equal,
because `@supports`/`@media` contribute nothing to specificity, only to WHEN
the inner rule applies. So only the sheet position decides between them,
and there is no fixed at-rule rank: the blocks that use the two rules
decide.

Module `aaa` (read first - alphabetically before `zzz`) writes `@media`
before `@supports` (its own intent: `@supports` overrides `@media`);
module `zzz` writes the opposite (its own intent: `@media` overrides
`@supports`).

  $ cat > aaa_media_then_supports.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css ("@media (min-width:600px){._a_8mediacol{color:blue;}}", "_a_8mediacol", "0,1,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css ("@supports (display:grid){._a_7suppcol{color:red;}}", "_a_7suppcol", "0,1,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(3, "", [0; 1])]]
  > EOF

  $ cat > zzz_supports_then_media.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css ("@supports (display:grid){._a_7suppcol{color:red;}}", "_a_7suppcol", "0,1,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css ("@media (min-width:600px){._a_8mediacol{color:blue;}}", "_a_8mediacol", "0,1,0 own", "color", 1, false)]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(3, "", [0; 1])]]
  > EOF

The blocks disagree: generate warns and keeps definition order (`aaa`'s),
in both CLI orders:

  $ styled-ppx.generate aaa_media_then_supports.ml zzz_supports_then_media.ml
  styled-ppx: block aaa_media_then_supports.ml:3 and block zzz_supports_then_media.ml:3 put two competing rules in opposite orders (@media (min-width:600px){._a_8mediacol{color:blue;}} and @supports (display:grid){._a_7suppcol{color:red;}}); the sheet keeps their definition order
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  @media (min-width:600px){._a_8mediacol{color:blue;}}
  @supports (display:grid){._a_7suppcol{color:red;}}

  $ styled-ppx.generate zzz_supports_then_media.ml aaa_media_then_supports.ml
  styled-ppx: block aaa_media_then_supports.ml:3 and block zzz_supports_then_media.ml:3 put two competing rules in opposite orders (@media (min-width:600px){._a_8mediacol{color:blue;}} and @supports (display:grid){._a_7suppcol{color:red;}}); the sheet keeps their definition order
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  @media (min-width:600px){._a_8mediacol{color:blue;}}
  @supports (display:grid){._a_7suppcol{color:red;}}

With only `zzz`'s block, its order holds:

  $ styled-ppx.generate zzz_supports_then_media.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  @supports (display:grid){._a_7suppcol{color:red;}}
  @media (min-width:600px){._a_8mediacol{color:blue;}}
